    "result_text": "Done. Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing, including both new membership-tier tests).\n\n**Change summary** \u2014 I followed the existing derived-field pattern (`membershipNumber`) to keep structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line to `toOwnerDto` and a small, self-contained `membershipTier(Owner)` default method:\n   ```java\n   default String membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n       boolean silver = Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount()) && owner.getEmail() != null;\n       return silver ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nI placed the logic in the small `OwnerMapper` interface rather than the large `Owner` entity \u2014 the mapper's low surrounding complexity (WMC_other) makes this the cheaper edit under the cost model, and it reuses the class already responsible for deriving DTO fields.",
